fix(run): reject a missing ELF in the driver, not via the engine

`andesim run --mode fast <missing>.elf` handed the missing path straight to
qemu, which failed with the cryptic "Unable to find the RISC-V BIOS ...".
Root cause: abs_elf resolved the path with fs::absolute -- a pure lexical op
that succeeds on a non-existent path -- and never checked the file exists.

Add the existence check to abs_elf, the one resolver fast/cycle/cycle-gdb all
share, so a missing ELF now fails up front with a clear
"andesim run --mode <m>: ELF not found: <path>" (exit 2) before any engine is
spawned. run_hybrid already had its own inline existence check with the same
message; route it through abs_elf too, so all four run paths share one check
(output byte-identical) instead of duplicating it.

Test: tests/andes_sim/test_andes_sim_missing_elf.sh asserts fast, cycle, and
hybrid each fail with "ELF not found" and never reach qemu's BIOS error.

